  "english": "20. Monday [Bch - Tone 2]. King Theodosius, and the Holy Infants of Ephesus.\n21. Tuesday [Gch - Tone 3]. Kyriakos and Yughita, and Gordios, Polyeuctus, and Grigoris.\n23. Thursday [Ech - Tone 5]. Vahan of Goghtn, and Eugenia the virgin, and her father Philip, and the others.\n25. Saturday [Shb]. Patriarchs Athanasius and Cyril.\n26. Sunday [Kir]. Second. [Tone 6 / gky] Canticle [Harts]: \"Who today was sacrificed\" (Aysor zenav).\n27. Monday [Bsh]. Eugenius, Macarius, etc.\n28. Tuesday [Gch]. Andrew the General and his army, etc.\n30. Thursday [Esh]. Adrian and his wife Anatolia, etc.\n\n[Unintelligible symbols/letters]\n\nFebruary\n1. Saturday [Shb]. Gregory the Theologian.\n2. Sunday [Kir]. Third. Barekendan [Eve] of the Fast of Catechumens.\n9. Sunday [Kir]. Saint Sargis.\n14. Friday [Ur]. Presentation of the Lord [Tyarnndaraj].\n23. Sunday [Kir]. Tone 8 [Dk]. Great Barekendan [Eve of Great Lent]. See in the First Volume up to Vardavar, keeping the order of this place.\n\nApril\n7. Monday [Bch]. Tone 3 [Bz]. Great [Monday] - and the Feast of the Annunciation of the Holy Virgin.\n13. Sunday [Kir]. Tone 1 [Az]. Easter: Day of the Resurrection of Christ. See according to the order in the First Volume.\n\nMay\n22. Thursday [Ech]. Tone 8 [Dk]. Ascension of Christ. And the rest according to the order.\n\nJune\n1. Sunday [Kir]. Tone 2 [Ak]. Descent of the Holy Spirit [Pentecost]. Barekendan of the Eliastic [Elijah] Fast.\n8. Sunday [Kir]. Tone 1 [Az]. First. Beginning of the Sundays of the Resurrection. Canticle [Harts] Tone 1 [ad]: \"Who came for salvation\" (Or ekir i prkutyun).\n\nJuly\nSunday [Kir]. Tone 3 [Bz]. Vardavar [Transfiguration]. The dispensation of eating meat [utikh] is three weeks. See this period up to the Barekendan of the Assumption of the Mother of God in the First Volume; only look here for the order of the Resurrection Canticles [Harts].\nSunday [Kir]. Tone 2 [Ak]. Second. Canticle [Harts] Tone 4 [bz]: \"Who descended from heaven\" (Or i yerkunits ijer). Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 2 [ak]: \"You were sent from the Father\" (Araketsar i hore).\nSunday [Kir]. Tone 1 [Az]. Third. Canticle [Harts] Tone 4 [bk]: \"Who by the heavenly hosts\" (Or yerknayyin zinvorutyants).\nSunday [Kir]. Tone 8 [Dk]. Fourth. Canticle [Harts] Tone 5 [gz]: \"We glorify you\" (Paravoremp zkhez). Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 8 [dk]: \"When they came\" (Yorzham ekin) and \"The angel descended\" (Ej hreshtakn). Barekendan of the Fast of the Holy Mother of God.\nMonday [Bsh]. Tone 1 [Az]: Fast of the Holy Mother of God. Canticle [Harts] Tone 4 [bz]: \"Blessed Lord God\" (Orhneal ter ast).\nSunday [Kir]. Tone 8 [Dz]. Assumption of the Holy Mother of God. The dispensation of eating meat [utikh] is three weeks. See according to the order in the First Volume.\n\n[Unintelligible letters/symbols]\n\nSeptember\nSunday [Kir]. Tone 4 [Bk]. Fourth. Canticle [Harts] Tone 6 [gk]: \"Inexpressible\" (Anchareli). Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 4 [bk]: \"Christ is risen\" (Kristos yareav). Barekendan of the Fast of the Holy Cross.\nMonday [Bch]. Tone 5 [Gz]. Fast. Feast of the Birth of the Holy Virgin from Anna.\nTuesday [Gsh]. Tone 6 [Gk]. Fast. Canticle [Harts] Tone 4 [bk]: \"The captive youths\" (Mankunkn gerealk).\nSunday [Kir]. Tone 3 [Bz]. Exaltation of the Holy Cross. See up to the tenth Sunday in the First Volume; but look for the canticles of the martyrs and of the fasts, the Resurrection Evening Hymns [Hambartsis], and the tone of the days in Year-letter [N], keeping the months.\n\nNovember\nSunday [Kir]. Tone 2 [Ak]. Tenth. Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 2 [ak]: \"Wonderful angel\" (Skancheli hreshtakn), to the end. Barekendan of the Hisnak [Advent].",
